# The orphan findings ledger is append-only: every branch adds its own
# block at the end and nothing edits another's. Git's default merge treats
# two appends at the same offset as a conflict, so every branch that
# recorded a finding had to hand-resolve the same non-conflict — several
# times a day once two sessions are working at once.
#
# `union` keeps both sides' lines, which for an append-only ledger is not a
# compromise but the correct answer: losing either block would be losing a
# recorded finding.
docs/reviews/orphan-findings.md merge=union
